WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Read a GPU instance specification as a complete system.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.160
Start with the exact accelerator model, count, architecture, and VRAM.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.200
VRAM constrains model weights, context cache, batch size, and training state.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.680
Two instances advertised as one GPU can deliver very different performance and software

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.400
compatibility.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.900
Confirm whether the device is dedicated, partitioned,

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.635
or shared and whether the intended framework supports it.

00:00:21.635 --> 00:00:25.629
Virtual CPU and system RAM support tokenization, data loading, decompression,

00:00:25.629 --> 00:00:27.500
preprocessing, and the serving application.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.709
Too few CPU cores can leave an expensive GPU waiting.

00:00:30.709 --> 00:00:34.100
Insufficient RAM can prevent model loading or force slow disk use.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.150
Examine local ephemeral storage and attached persistent-disk options separately.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.115
Ephemeral disks may be fast but disappear with the instance,

00:00:41.115 --> 00:00:44.405
while persistent disks survive and continue generating charges.

00:00:44.405 --> 00:00:48.670
Network specifications influence dataset movement, model downloads, distributed work,

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:49.980
and service response.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.700
Published maximum bandwidth may depend on instance size or traffic conditions.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.500
Region and availability zone affect latency to users and other services,

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.300
data-residency obligations, and whether a desired GPU can be provisioned.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.760
Place related compute and storage deliberately to avoid unnecessary transfer or cross-zone

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.400
charges.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.480
Hourly price is only the visible starting point.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.870
Check minimum billing increments, operating-system charges, discounts, interruption terms,

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.345
and storage and network rates.

00:01:14.345 --> 00:01:17.020
Before building automation around an instance type,

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.238
verify account quotas and actual capacity.

00:01:19.238 --> 00:01:23.420
A catalog listing does not guarantee that the GPU is available in the required region at

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.500
the required time.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.500
Maintain at least one acceptable alternative configuration for important work.
